cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Doppelstep in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Doppelstep: Zephyr RTOS stepper motor controller seen as a DYNAMIXEL smart servo"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Zephyr RTOS firmware that drives a two-phase stepper motor in closed-loop
  microstepping current control on the STMicroelectronics B-G431B-ESC1 and answers on the
  bus as a DYNAMIXEL XM430-W350 (Protocol 2.0), with an MCUboot bootloader, a simulated
  motor for software-in-the-loop tests, and a bench GUI.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vynohradov
    given-names: Anton
    email: avynohradov@systemfromscratch.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6965-0911"
    affiliation: SystemFromScratch®
repository-code: "https://github.com/SystemFromScratch/sfs-doppelstep"
url: "https://systemfromscratch.github.io/sfs-doppelstep/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - stepper motor
  - closed-loop microstepping
  - current control
  - Zephyr RTOS
  - DYNAMIXEL
  - ROS 2
  - STM32
  - MCUboot
  - software-in-the-loop
  - embedded firmware
